# Auto-registers TestDatabaseResetListener for every SpringApplication started in the test JVM,
# so it fires without each @SpringBootTest class needing to declare it. See the class itself for
# why it hooks ApplicationEnvironmentPreparedEvent instead of a JUnit extension.
#
# Nothing calls this file directly: SpringApplication's constructor scans the classpath for every
# file literally named META-INF/spring.factories and auto-registers whatever is listed here under
# the ApplicationListener key. It only exists on the test classpath (src/test/resources), which
# Maven never bundles into the packaged app, so this reset can't run outside a test JVM - not
# via a profile check, just because the file isn't on the classpath when the app runs normally.
org.springframework.context.ApplicationListener=\
com.starbuck.moneytracker.testsupport.TestDatabaseResetListener
